# Project Guidelines & Architecture

## Core Tech Stack

* **Framework:** Astro (`.astro` files)
* **Language:** TypeScript (Use standard TS types/interfaces in frontmatter)
* **Styling:** Tailwind CSS

## Design System & Styling Rules

* **Tailwind Configuration:** Ensure all custom colors and fonts below are properly extended in `tailwind.config.mjs` under the `theme.extend` object.
* **Strict Color Usage:** Apply theme colors using your custom Tailwind classes. Do **not** invent arbitrary hex codes or use default Tailwind colors.
  * **Accent Colors:** 
    * `#385da2` Blue
    * `#cd1e2b` Red
    * `#2d7d3f` Green
  * **Background Colors:**
    * `#fff` White
    * `#f4f5f6` Light Gray
    * `#cccabf` Mid Gray 1
    * `#474641` Mid Gray 2
    * `#292825` Dark Gray
    * `#33333d` Mid Dark
* **Typography:** Reference the custom fonts located in the `/public/fonts/` (or `/src/fonts/`) folder. Define these in the Tailwind config as primary font families (e.g., `font-sans`, `font-heading`).
* **Units:** Do not use `px` for font sizes — use `rem` instead. When the user specifies a value in `px`, always convert it to `rem` first (16px = 1rem) before applying it in code. **Exception:** border radius values may use `px`.
* **Container:** The max width of the content should be 1440px.

## Assets

* All image assets are hosted at https://assets.paprika-advertising.com. Import `asset()` from `src/lib/assets.ts` to build image URLs. Do not hardcode the CDN base in components.

## Responsive & Mobile-First Design

* **Desktop-First Approach:** Write styles for desktop screens by default, then layer on layout and style changes using Tailwind's breakpoint prefixes (`sm:`, `md:`, `lg:`, `xl:`).
* **Fluid Layouts:** Every component and page layout **must be responsive out of the box**. Do not build desktop-only layouts that overflow on smaller viewports.

## Component Architecture

* **File Structure:** Place all reusable `.astro` components in `src/components/`, page layouts in `src/layouts/`, and pages in `src/pages/`.
* **Islands Architecture:** Keep server-first rendering by default. Only use interactive client directives (`client:load`, `client:idle`, `client:visible`) when strictly necessary for JavaScript interactivity.

## Sanity CMS Editability

* **Every page section must be Sanity-editable.** Not only dynamic/list content — also section copy (headlines, body text, CTAs, labels) and images (including alt text).
* **Section reordering:** Page sections must be modeled so editors can reorder them in Sanity (e.g. an ordered array of section blocks).
* **Do not expose chrome that should stay code-owned.** Skip Sanity fields where editing does not make sense — e.g. main navigation, site-wide layout chrome, and similar structural UI. Prefer hardcoding those in the codebase.

## JavaScript Organization & Formatting

* **Modular Files:** Do **not** write monolithic `<script>` tags or massive single JS/TS files. Split logic into small, modular files organized logically in `src/scripts/` or alongside the component.
* **Header Comment Required:** Every JS/TS file **must** start with a brief 1–2 line comment explaining its core purpose. Don't add comments to other file types.

## Live Site Reference

* **Production website:** https://www.paprika-advertising.com/
* Agents may fetch this URL (and its pages) as a visual/content reference for layout, copy, structure, and design decisions when implementing or updating the site.

